{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 107, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 removed, the 0->2 path carries more of the signal, so upgrading edge 1 gives larger gains (experiments 4, 45, 58)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learnable conv with pooling loses capacity, and the drops are consistent across datasets (experiments 7, 66)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling removes the strongest op, as in experiment 78."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a pooling edge that may be a key connectivity path hurts badly (experiment 70, about -13 to -16 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a conv on the final edge into the output is costly (experiment 28, up to -12.6 on ImageNet16-120)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a parameter-free pool on the input edge for a 3x3 conv gives a big gain (experiments 10, 91)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is already none, removing edge 0 cuts off the node 1 and node 2 paths (experiment 38, about -3.5 to -11.6)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input->output edge where none exists helps, while replacing an existing conv or skip hurts (experiments 1, 25 versus 32, 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lo